==English==

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-|es}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy}} The moment when the sun appears to cross the [[celestial equator]] while tilting towards from the observer, taking place in March in the northern hemisphere and September in the southern hemisphere.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|spring equinox}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|autumnal equinox}}
* {{l|en|summer solstice}}
* {{l|en|winter solstice}}

